In article <1993Jun3.161748.4111@bmers95.bnr.ca> snelling@bnr.ca (Peter Snelling) writes:
>Elven mithril does not protect against level drains.  I've noticed that
>level draining happens fairly infrequently, however if you put of just
>elven mithril, and summon some Wraiths (hopefully in Wizard mode),
>eventually they will drain a level.

Here's the relevant code from mhitu.c.

/*      Next a cancellation factor      */
/*      Use ctmp when the cancellation factor takes into account certain
 *      armor's special magic protection.  Otherwise just use !mtmp->mcan.
 */
        armpro = 0;
        if (uarm && armpro < objects[uarm->otyp].a_can)
                armpro = objects[uarm->otyp].a_can;
        if (uarmc && armpro < objects[uarmc->otyp].a_can)
                armpro = objects[uarmc->otyp].a_can;
        ctmp = !mtmp->mcan && ((rn2(3) >= armpro) || !rn2(50));

Elven mithril coats have an .a_can of 3, as well as dwarven mithril, and many
cloaks have 2 or 3, so they should protect against special attacks most of the
time.
